A. Symplectic Hopf invariant
The Bogoliubov modes|w n(k)⟩, the columns of the
paraunitary Bogoliubov transformationW k, play the role
of the Bloch states akin to single-particle wave functions
in the conventional Hermitian case [43, 54]. We stress
that|w n(k)⟩denotes such a single-particle Bogoliubov
mode, a coefficient vector in the four-dimensional Nambu
space, and is not to be confused with a many-body Fock
state such as the multi-mode-squeezed-vacuum ground
state of the BBdG Hamiltonian (6). These Bogoliubov
modes|w n(k)⟩solve the eigenvalue problem
