C Classical vs Quantum on resonance
We have seen that the resonance poles can be used as a way to probe the difference
between the classical and the quantum theory. However, when we go to resonance, the
pole structure vanishes and needs to be resummed. In this section, we want to explain, in
the two examples of spins and harmonic oscillators that we have seen in 3.1 and 4.1, how
the resonant Hamiltonian leads to differences between the classical and quantum theories
in a way that is observable by measuring the correlators of the theory.
