In contrast, interactions of a fast up wave and a slow down wave exhibit much larger
height ratios. Their profile describes an absorb-emit interaction where the slow wave is first
absorbed by the fast wave, producing a symmetrical peak atx= 0 with side troughs that
form “holes”, from which the fast wave then emerges and emits the slow wave behind it.
The net height of this wave profile is given by the height of the peak minus the depth of the
3
