the reflectionu→−uof this profile.
The ratio of the net height to the height of the up wave approaches 2.41 when the two
waves have approximately the same speedr→1; it decreases to 2 atr= 1.5, and continues
to decrease to 1 asrgoes to infinity (see Fig. 3). Thus, rogue-like waves are produced in
this type of collision, but only for a small range of relative speeds, 1< v 1/v2 <2.25. The
shape of the rogue-like wave having a maximum net-height ratio is shown in Fig. 4.
